DEFERRED SCOPE EXPANSION — `autoharness.verify_workspace._derive_template_variables` does not supply every `{{VAR}}` the shipped templates actually use, so rendering leaves UNRESOLVED placeholders in the output. Per this project's own contract ("Unresolved variables in output files indicate an installation error", .github/copilot-instructions.md) this is an install-correctness defect.

MEASURED (Stage read-only spike, 2026-08-20, using this workspace's own manifest/config/profile/registry):
- _ship.agent.md.tmpl        -> 6 unresolved, incl. {{ESCALATION_FAMILY}}, {{ESCALATION_PROVIDER}}, {{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}, {{CONTINUOUS_LEARNING_PROMOTION_THRESHOLD}}
- _stage.agent.md.tmpl       -> 4 unresolved, incl. {{ESCALATION_FAMILY}}, {{ESCALATION_PROVIDER}}, {{ESCALATION_REASONING_EFFORT}}
- _orchestrator.agent.md.tmpl-> 10 unresolved, incl. {{ORCHESTRATOR_FAMILY}}, {{ORCHESTRATOR_PROVIDER}}, {{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}
- github-pr-automation.instructions.md.tmpl -> 1 unresolved: {{FORMAT_CHECK_COMMAND}}

Notably FORMAT_CHECK_COMMAND is absent from the derived variable map ENTIRELY, and LINT_COMMAND derives to the EMPTY STRING — yet the installed dogfood copy contains real values ("# no format check command configured", 'markdownlint "**/*.md"'). The escalation route (gpt-5.6-sol / openai / high) and the default branch are both plainly present in .autoharness/config.yaml, so the values exist and are simply not being derived.

OUT OF SCOPE per P-021 C1: discovered during Stage's own spike for 6D62077C (template/dogfood render parity) while rendering templates to measure divergence. It was NOT part of the authorised scope, and it touches a DIFFERENT surface — variable derivation / install correctness in src/autoharness/verify_workspace.py — rather than the maintenance-contract question 6D62077C asked. "Discovered in the same investigation" and "same file" do not make it in scope. Deliberately excluded from shipment 145-S.

Source refs: origin stash 6D62077C; spike docs/decisions/2026-08-20-template-dogfood-render-parity-spike.md (finding F5); feature 137-F; shipment 145-S; PR: N/A (pre-PR Stage discovery); review-thread ID: N/A (no thread exists).

requires deliberation: yes — the fix must decide whether the derivation gap is (a) missing derivation logic, (b) intentionally optional variables that should be documented as such, or (c) a sign that verify_workspace's renderer is not the install-time renderer and should not be treated as authoritative for parity at all. Option (c) would also retroactively affect how the 137-F parity contract is interpreted.
